<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 20 June, from 451 to 1991.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Refugee Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Designated by the UN General Assembly in 2001 to coincide with the 50th anniversary of the 1951 Refugee Convention, World Refugee Day honours the courage and resilience of the more than 100 million forcibly displaced people worldwide.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/451">451 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,575 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aetius checks Attila at the Catalaunian Plains</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> to a halt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, on a date traditionally given as 20 June. Attila withdrew, and invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1180">1180 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">846 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Battle of Uji begins the Genpei War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The First Battle of Uji followed Prince Mochihito and Minamoto no Yorimasa's plan to raise an army to overthrow the Taira clan, and an edict urging the Minamoto clan, temples and shrines to revolt. It began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genpei-war">Genpei War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genpei-war">Genpei War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1210">1210 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">816 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michael I Komnenos Doukas of Epirus becomes a vassal of Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A treaty negotiated by envoys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-i-komnenos-doukas">Michael I Komnenos Doukas</a>, founder of the Despotate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, was confirmed by oath, making him a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. He granted the Venetians trading privileges and tax exemptions and promised an annual tribute.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">Vassal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1756">1756 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">270 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British captives are confined in the 'Black Hole of Calcutta'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Nawab of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a>, British prisoners were held overnight in a tiny guardroom, where many died. The numbers are disputed, but the story fuelled British retaliation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1789">1789 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Third Estate swears the Tennis Court Oath</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Locked out of their hall, deputies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> met in a royal tennis court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> and vowed not to separate until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> had a constitution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1837">1837 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">189 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Victoria becomes queen at the age of 18</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Victoria was woken at Kensington Palace with news that William IV had died. Her 63-year reign saw industrial growth and the expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US and Soviet Union agree to set up a hotline</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis">Cuban Missile Crisis</a>, the agreement created a direct teletype link between Washington and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. Popularly called the 'red <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telephone">telephone</a>', it was never a telephone.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bundestag votes to move Germany's government to Berlin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By 338 votes to 320, the parliament of reunified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a> as the seat of government. The move was completed in 1999.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 20 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-iii-vasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sigismund III Vasa</span><span class="tp">1566–1632</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-ii-duke-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-emmanuel-ii-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles Emmanuel II, Duke of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1634–1675</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/theobald-wolfe-tone"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/theobald-wolfe-tone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Theobald Wolfe Tone</span><span class="tp">1763–1798</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-douglas-5th-earl-of-selkirk"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-douglas-5th-earl-of-selkirk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Douglas, 5th Earl of Selkirk</span><span class="tp">1771–1820</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jean-moulin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jean-moulin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jean Moulin</span><span class="tp">1899–1943</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/xanana-gusmao"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/xanana-gusmao.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Xanana Gusmão</span><span class="tp">b. 1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gotabaya-rajapaksa"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Gotabaya Rajapaksa</span><span class="tp">b. 1949</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 20 June <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-belgrano.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel Belgrano</span><span class="tp">1770–1820</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-of-the-united-kingdom"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-iv-of-the-united-kingdom.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William IV of the United Kingdom</span><span class="tp">1765–1837</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hijikata-toshizo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hijikata-toshizo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hijikata Toshizō</span><span class="tp">1835–1869</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georges-lemaitre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georges-lemaitre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georges Lemaître</span><span class="tp">1894–1966</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
